<title>IRAN: Iran pilots take off for higher wages abroad-paper.</title>
<headline>Iran pilots take off for higher wages abroad-paper.</headline>
<dateline>TEHRAN 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>More than 10 percent of pilots and co-pilots at the Iranian flag carrier Iran Air have emigrated in the past year in search of higher wages, a newspaper said on Monday.</p>
<p>It quoted several Iran Air pilots as saying about 50 colleagues had emigrated to Malaysia, South Korea, Japan and Luxembourg where they could receive much higher wages than the maximum 1.5 million rials ($500) per month in Iran. Pilots' wages are considerably higher than average salaries in Iran.</p>
<p>There was no independent confirmation of the report.</p>
<p>The pilots, who were not named, said Iran Air currently had 400 pilots and co-pilots after some 200 had emigrated since the 1979 Islamic revolution, the newspaper added. ($1=3,000 rials at the official exchange rate)</p>
</text>
